course: dictionary
lesson: 1249
title: Burdock and the burrs that hitch a ride
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Burdock is a plant. It is a tall weed with big leaves, and its seed heads are round and prickly. These prickly seed heads are called burrs. «Some hitch a ride: burdock burrs hook onto your dog's fur after a walk.» To hitch a ride means to travel by being carried along, without driving yourself.
explain: Context gives you clues. Read «Some seeds hook onto animals' fur, like burdock burrs.» The word hook tells you that a burr is something that catches and holds on, like a little hook. So a burr must be a prickly seed case that sticks to things.
explain: Look at the list in this sentence: «dandelion seeds fly on little parachutes, burdock burrs hook onto fur, coconuts float, and berries are eaten by birds.» Each part shows a different way seeds travel. Burdock is one example in that list of seed travel methods.
explain: Check your guess by swapping it into the sentence. "Burrs hook onto your dog's fur" still makes sense, so your meaning fits. For a plant name like burdock, a dictionary or a picture will confirm it.
fact: A burdock is a tall weed with big leaves.
fact: Its round, prickly seed heads are called burrs.
fact: Burrs stick to clothes and animal fur, which carries the seeds away from the parent plant.
fact: Burdock burrs inspired the invention of Velcro.
fact: In the UK, dandelion and burdock is a traditional fizzy drink.
exercise: What is a burdock? | A type of fizzy drink only | A tree that grows coconuts | *A tall weed with big leaves and prickly seed heads | A small bird that eats berries
exercise: «Some hitch a ride: burdock burrs hook onto your dog's fur.» What does hitch a ride mean? | To buy a new bike | To grow very tall | To dig a deep hole | *To travel by being carried along
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Some seeds hook onto animals' fur, like burdock burrs.» that means a prickly seed case. | hook | animals | *burrs | fur
test: Why do burdock burrs stick to a dog after a walk? | They are hungry | They want to be cleaned | They are made of wool | *So the seeds can travel far from the parent plant
test: In «birds eat berries and drop the seeds far away», how do these seeds travel? | Sticking to fur | *Being eaten by birds and dropped far away | Floating on water | Flying on little parachutes
exam: Which fizzy drink is traditionally made with burdock in the UK? | Cola | Ginger beer | *Dandelion and burdock | Lemonade
